{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"## Offline eval of the grouping prompt (2026-11-02), Gerrit change 3242\n\nRan the production prompt `plan-review-fix-unit-grouping` through the real runner (Bedrock, the standard model class `_verifier_cfg` resolves, temperature 0) over the 8 bakeoff verdicts that hold the 24 judge-confirmed duplicate groups (same verdict selection as `.rebar/scratch/a85e3cd3-prox/prox.py`). Script: `.rebar/scratch/a85e3cd3-snowyowl/eval_grouping.py` in the worktree; results in `eval-results.json` beside it. The call saw the findings only, as in production (no plan text).\n\n**Production mode — BLOCKING findings only (what ships):**\n- Judged duplicate pairs with both members blocking: 15. Grouped: **13 of 15** (87%).\n- Other blocking pairs in the same verdicts: 104. Falsely merged: **3** (2.9%).\n- Invalid answers (fail-open path taken): 0 of 8 calls.\n- Per run (blocking findings / judged pairs / hit / false merge): rfi 7/4/4/0, carbon 7/4/4/0, dso-legacy 4/0/0/0, uswds 8/2/2/0, opensearch 7/1/1/1, mn-deed 4/1/1/0, dso-strata 4/1/1/0, spree 5/2/0/2.\n- Both misses and 2 of the 3 false merges are in rb-spree: the model regrouped 4 blocking findings across the two judged groups (fee2ecdefb4a472fd with f9787d46f01fa1024; fe9362212ee777e1b with f4bd59683171f9ef2) instead of the judged (f4bd59683171f9ef2, fee2ecdefb4a472fd) and (f808aa9b1ff1a1a44, f9787d46f01fa1024). The third false merge is java-opensearch f92b6304f04d09171 + faf9a816e511a41da (two AC-verifiability findings).\n\n**Capability probe — blocking + advisory together (not shipped; advisory is out of scope):**\n- 39 judged pairs, 27 grouped (69%); 17 false merges among 1,192 other pairs (1.4%).\n- 1 of 8 answers was rejected by validation (jira-dso-legacy: the model put one finding in two groups, which the bridging finding f979dd7afcdc2675a invites); the fail-open path stamped nothing, as designed.\n\nGroup stamps are counted at pair level: a false merge pair means two findings would share a `group_id` and the CLI would fold one under the other; both still block and stay in the sidecar."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793658782208821001,"uuid":"2d9b8449-8f51-4710-97b0-5ec4adc6b6dd"}